cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PSDAT — Power System Dynamic Analysis Toolbox"
message: "If you use this software or the accompanying textbook, please cite them as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Abdulrahman
    given-names: Ismael Khorshed
    email: ismael.abdulrahman@epu.edu.iq
    affiliation: "Erbil Polytechnic University, Erbil, Kurdistan Region, Iraq"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ismaelabdulrahman/psdat-book"
url: "https://ismaelabdulrahman.github.io/psdat-book/"
abstract: >-
  PSDAT is a transparent, open, education-first toolbox for the static and
  dynamic analysis of renewable-dominated power systems, with matched Python
  and MATLAB implementations and a free Android companion app. It is the
  toolbox behind the graduate textbook "Power System Dynamics of
  Renewable-Dominated Grids: A Transparent, Computational Approach with PSDAT".
keywords:
  - power system dynamics
  - transient stability
  - small-signal stability
  - grid-forming converters
  - inverter-based resources
  - renewable energy
  - FACTS
  - phasor measurement units
  - open-source education
